      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel anxious about cutting back on something you've been relying on, like water, especially if you're experiencing persistent thirst. Taking an excess of electrolyte powder could lead to an imbalance or other complications, considering the already indicated overhydration. It's a good approach to first see if you can gradually reduce your water intake while integrating an appropriate amount of electrolytes, with the aim to avoid sudden changes that stress your body. However, without clinical evaluation, it's challenging to determine what's the most effective and safe approach for your specific condition. If you're feeling uncomfortable about this, a healthcare professional, even if just for reassurance or minor advice, could be beneficial. Your health and well-being should always come first and professional advice can prevent potential risks with self-diagnosis and treatment.",
